# OpenProninx Hybrid GPT Disk Image Layout (PRONINX.img)

OpenProninx disk images use a Hybrid GPT layout created via `tools/mkimage.sh` that boots across both legacy BIOS and UEFI firmware:

```
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Sector 0: Protective MBR / stage_1.S (relocates to 0x600, parses GPT, loads stage2)|
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Sectors 1-33: GPT Header & Partition Entry Array Table                           |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Partition 1: EFI System Partition (ESP, Type EF00, FAT32, ~64 MiB)               |
|   - /EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI (Clang/LLD compiled UEFI 2.10 loader)                  |
|   - /fnu/kernel           (ELF64 kernel binary)                                  |
|   - /fnu/ramdisk          (ELF/RAMDisk rootfs boot module)                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Partition 2: fnu-boot (Type GUID 7B589DA3-BDC2-4F6C-8028-FC43D46C5953, ~1 MiB)   |
|   - Raw binary stage2 (realprot NetBSD thunk, FAT32 reader, VBE/EDID, A20, ELF64)|
|   - Attribute: LEGACY_BIOS_BOOTABLE                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Partition 3: fnu-root (Type 8300, ~32 MiB)                                       |
|   - Persistent root filesystem / storage partition                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Secondary / Backup GPT Table (last 33 sectors of the disk)                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Boot Flow Comparison

### BIOS Boot Chain:
1. BIOS loads MBR (stage_1.S) at `0x7C00`.
2. stage_1 relocates itself to `0x600`, parses GPT partition entries, locates partition with `FNUBOOT_GUID` / `LEGACY_BIOS_BOOTABLE`.
3. stage_1 uses INT 13h extensions to load stage2 into memory.
4. stage2 activates A20, queries VBE/EDID / coreboot tables, reads `/fnu/kernel` and `/fnu/ramdisk` from the FAT32 ESP, builds PML4/PDPT/PD page tables with DMAP, populates `struct bootinfo`, and transitions the CPU into 64-bit Long Mode.

### UEFI Boot Chain:
1. UEFI firmware executes `/EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI`.
2. Loader discovers GOP framebuffer, allocates memory map, reads `/fnu/kernel` and `/fnu/ramdisk` into memory.
3. Calls `ExitBootServices`, preserves EFI Runtime Services pointers in `bootinfo`, and jumps directly to 64-bit kernel entry.
